### Step 1: Add the safety nets to application.properties
Since AppConfig is gone, we need to tell Spring's auto-configuration engine to handle your dates properly and to ignore garbage JSON fields from React.
Open your src/main/resources/application.properties file and paste these exact lines at the bottom:
```properties
# 1. Format dates as readable strings (e.g., "24/06/2026") instead of weird timestamp arrays
spring.jackson.serialization.write-dates-as-timestamps=false

# 2. THE ULTIMATE SAFETY NETS: Stop Jackson from crashing on React's bad payloads
spring.jackson.deserialization.fail-on-unknown-properties=false
spring.jackson.deserialization.accept-empty-string-as-null-object=true

```
### Step 2: Fix CacheConfig.java (Use Spring's Default Mapper)
Because we deleted your custom config, Spring Boot will now automatically generate a perfectly safe, default ObjectMapper in the background. We need to tell your Redis Cache to use *that* safe mapper, instead of creating its own rogue strict parser.
Update your CacheConfig.java bean to look exactly like this:
```java
package com.fincore.VoucherService.config;

import lombok.extern.slf4j.Slf4j;
import org.springframework.cache.annotation.EnableCaching;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Bean;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Configuration;
import com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.ObjectMapper; // <-- ADD IMPORT

@Configuration
@EnableCaching
@Slf4j
public class CacheConfig {

    @Bean
    public org.springframework.cache.CacheManager cacheManager(
            org.springframework.data.redis.connection.RedisConnectionFactory connectionFactory,
            ObjectMapper springDefaultMapper) { // <-- 1. Spring Boot automatically injects the safe mapper here!

        log.info("CACHE_CONFIG_INIT | Using Redis-backed CacheManager for K8s compatibility");

        org.springframework.data.redis.cache.RedisCacheConfiguration config =
                org.springframework.data.redis.cache.RedisCacheConfiguration.defaultCacheConfig()
                        .entryTtl(java.time.Duration.ofMinutes(30))
                        .disableCachingNullValues()
                        .serializeValuesWith(
                                org.springframework.data.redis.serializer.RedisSerializationContext.SerializationPair
                                        // 2. Pass Spring's safe mapper into Redis
                                        .fromSerializer(new org.springframework.data.redis.serializer.GenericJackson2JsonRedisSerializer(springDefaultMapper)));

        return org.springframework.data.redis.cache.RedisCacheManager.builder(connectionFactory)
                .cacheDefaults(config)
                .withCacheConfiguration("notification_configs",
                        config.entryTtl(java.time.Duration.ofHours(1)))
                .build();
    }
}

```
### Step 3: Stop the GlobalExceptionHandler Blindfold
We need to stop your Exception Handler from hiding JSON errors behind the "Internal storage access failure" message.
Open GlobalExceptionHandler.java and paste this block *anywhere* inside the class:
```java
    // Catches JSON parsing crashes BEFORE they fall into the generic IOException bucket
    @ExceptionHandler(org.springframework.http.converter.HttpMessageNotReadableException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<com.fincore.VoucherService.Dto.ApiErrorResponseDto> handleJsonParseError(org.springframework.http.converter.HttpMessageNotReadableException ex, jakarta.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest request) {
        log.error("JSON_PARSE_ERROR | Path: {} | Reason: {}", request.getRequestURI(), ex.getMostSpecificCause().getMessage());
        
        // This gives you a 400 Bad Request with the EXACT reason, instead of a 500 IO Error.
        return buildResponse(
                org.springframework.http.HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST, 
                "Malformed JSON Payload", 
                "The server could not read the request. Reason: " + ex.getMostSpecificCause().getMessage(), 
                request.getRequestURI(), 
                null
        );
    }

```
